WEBVTT

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.652 --> 00:00:06.030
Today we talk about three lash styles that clients very often bring photos of:

00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:08.830
mega volume, wispy, and wet look.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.230
These three look stunning in photos.

00:00:11.496 --> 00:00:15.135
But they are also the styles most likely to damage natural lashes,

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:17.310
if the technician just chases the photo.

00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:20.649
Understand them properly, and you can make them beautiful,

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:22.990
while the client's natural lashes stay healthy.

00:00:23.513 --> 00:00:25.157
First, mega volume.

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:27.317
That is volume at its fullest.

00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:31.317
In the volume lesson, we made fans of two to six lashes.

00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:34.942
With mega volume, each fan has even more lashes,

00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:37.717
and every one of them is as fine as silk.

00:00:38.253 --> 00:00:43.317
The result is a very full, very dark lash line, like a soft eyeliner.

00:00:43.742 --> 00:00:48.471
Because the lashes are so fine, it looks full, yet the tips stay soft,

00:00:48.421 --> 00:00:51.077
not stiff like a strip of false lashes.

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:52.357
But remember well:

00:00:52.468 --> 00:00:56.997
however many lashes a fan has, it still goes on a single natural lash.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:58.855
Wispy is different.

00:00:59.097 --> 00:01:01.655
It is a textured style that looks like feathers.

00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:05.735
The technician makes a base layer of short, soft fans.

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:09.655
Then, evenly spaced among them, come the spikes:

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:13.804
lashes closed together into a single point, or a single lash,

00:01:13.754 --> 00:01:15.495
longer than the base layer.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.700
The long points stand out from the base layer,

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:22.215
creating an uneven edge with a rhythm, which looks very soft.

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:26.549
And wet look means lashes that look as if they have just been in water.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.229
Instead of open fans, we use closed fans:

00:01:30.486 --> 00:01:34.949
the lashes pressed together into points, placed close together along the lash line.

00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:38.629
The lashes look glossy, separated into clear points.

00:01:39.055 --> 00:01:43.669
This style suits clients who like a sharp, defined look, rather than a fluffy one.

00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:47.360
Why are these three styles so likely to damage lashes?

00:01:47.751 --> 00:01:49.480
Because to make them dramatic,

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.560
technicians tend to add more lashes and more thickness.

00:01:52.733 --> 00:01:56.480
To make wispy really stand out, they make the spikes really long.

00:01:56.902 --> 00:02:00.480
But the weight rule from the classic and volume lessons still holds:

00:02:00.706 --> 00:02:03.520
what a natural lash can carry does not change.

00:02:03.697 --> 00:02:05.520
Here, it matters even more.

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:10.320
Because each fan has more lashes, and each spike is longer than the base layer.

00:02:10.943 --> 00:02:16.731
So the full version of these styles is only for strong, long, thick natural lashes.

00:02:16.988 --> 00:02:22.251
Fine, short or sparse natural lashes can still have them, but in a lighter version:

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.571
fans with fewer lashes, shorter spikes, and fewer spikes.

00:02:26.998 --> 00:02:30.731
It still reads as that style, without overloading the natural lashes.

00:02:31.076 --> 00:02:34.091
Looking closely, most clients will not see the difference.

00:02:34.265 --> 00:02:35.691
But their natural lashes will.

00:02:36.303 --> 00:02:38.821
With mega volume, two things are essential.

00:02:39.323 --> 00:02:42.370
First, use the finest lashes your lash brand makes,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.661
following the guide chart of the brand.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:48.981
Many lashes that are also thick make the fan several times heavier.

00:02:49.527 --> 00:02:51.381
Second, very little glue.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.893
The more lashes in a fan, the smaller and neater its base must be,

00:02:55.843 --> 00:02:58.181
and it touches only a tiny bit of glue.

00:02:58.497 --> 00:03:03.061
A wide base with too much glue is heavy, stiff, and prone to stickies.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.457
Spikes have their own difficulty.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.377
A spike is a closed fan:

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.417
the lashes lie close together, so it looks slim.

00:03:10.914 --> 00:03:13.537
But its weight is still the total of all the lashes in it.

00:03:13.946 --> 00:03:16.647
And because the spike is longer than the base layer,

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:18.737
it presses on the root like a long lever:

00:03:19.002 --> 00:03:21.617
the longer it is, the harder the root has to work.

00:03:21.786 --> 00:03:24.313
So spikes should go on the strongest natural lashes,

00:03:24.263 --> 00:03:27.217
and should not be made too long compared with the base layer.

00:03:27.918 --> 00:03:30.427
A beautiful wispy set is all about rhythm.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.092
The spikes are evenly spaced, their lengths follow the lash map,

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:36.827
and they usually get longer toward the outer corner.

00:03:37.086 --> 00:03:39.787
Spikes too dense, and the texture is lost:

00:03:40.123 --> 00:03:41.227
it just looks messy.

00:03:41.407 --> 00:03:43.707
Too sparse, and it looks unfinished.

00:03:44.136 --> 00:03:48.506
That is why wispy always needs a map, with the spike positions marked in advance,

00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:50.107
as in the lash mapping lesson.

00:03:50.636 --> 00:03:52.837
Before you start, consult carefully.

00:03:53.175 --> 00:03:56.757
Show the client example photos, and ask how dramatic she wants it.

00:03:57.078 --> 00:03:59.157
Moderate, or really striking.

00:03:59.581 --> 00:04:00.757
Then explain clearly.

00:04:01.186 --> 00:04:05.962
The more dramatic the style, the more easily gaps show when lashes shed naturally,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.037
so the client needs regular refills,

00:04:08.216 --> 00:04:09.797
usually after two to three weeks.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:15.957
And how long the lashes last depends on healthy natural lashes and on how the client looks after them at home,

00:04:16.146 --> 00:04:17.797
not on the number of lashes.

00:04:18.456 --> 00:04:20.837
There is another reason to keep refill appointments:

00:04:20.944 --> 00:04:24.837
as the natural lash grows, it carries the fan away from the lid.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.155
The heavier the fan, the more easily it turns,

00:04:28.105 --> 00:04:30.997
twists and pulls on the lash as it grows out.

00:04:31.247 --> 00:04:34.357
At a refill, the grown out lashes need to be removed.

00:04:35.027 --> 00:04:36.853
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:04:37.103 --> 00:04:40.693
A client has mega volume for the first time, and loves it.

00:04:41.122 --> 00:04:44.453
By the second or third refill, the technician notices:

00:04:44.735 --> 00:04:48.921
natural lashes bending down, some twisted or pointing the wrong way,

00:04:48.871 --> 00:04:52.693
and scattered gaps where natural lashes have fallen out early.

00:04:53.121 --> 00:04:54.533
Those are signs of overload.

00:04:54.881 --> 00:04:57.093
The natural lashes are crying for help.

00:04:57.756 --> 00:04:59.967
At that point, a good technician stops,

00:04:59.917 --> 00:05:02.625
and does not keep going just to match the photo.

00:05:03.028 --> 00:05:03.985
They lighten the set:

00:05:04.324 --> 00:05:07.975
fewer lashes in each fan, shorter lengths, fewer spikes,

00:05:07.925 --> 00:05:10.225
and they explain to the client why.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.811
After a few lighter refills, the natural lashes recover,

00:05:13.761 --> 00:05:16.705
and only then do you think about going fuller again.

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:19.025
The client may be disappointed at first.

00:05:19.211 --> 00:05:23.665
But a year later, she still has lashes to work on, and she is still your client.

00:05:24.344 --> 00:05:25.678
A few more short points.

00:05:26.107 --> 00:05:29.281
Tweezers are cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:05:29.231 --> 00:05:32.238
as in the lesson on handling tools after each client.

00:05:32.753 --> 00:05:34.398
Glue can cause allergies:

00:05:34.639 --> 00:05:38.718
for the signs and what to do, see the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:39.066 --> 00:05:43.598
And if the eyes are red or inflamed, see the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:05:44.258 --> 00:05:45.055
To sum up:

00:05:45.163 --> 00:05:48.158
mega volume, wispy and wet look are all beautiful,

00:05:48.108 --> 00:05:51.455
when the natural lashes are strong enough to carry them.

00:05:52.044 --> 00:05:54.895
A great technician is not the one who can make the fullest set.

00:05:55.244 --> 00:05:56.975
It is the one who knows when to stop.

00:05:57.476 --> 00:06:00.175
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step.

00:06:00.522 --> 00:06:03.135
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:03.308 --> 00:06:04.175
See you next time.
